CORE
test.c
--nondet-volatile-write-model data:observe_data --nondet-volatile-write-model cmd:observe_cmd --mmio-weak-variable cmd
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
data committed before GO: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
Per-register memory-type tagging: the data register is strongly ordered (only
cmd is marked weak), so the write to data is observed in program order before
the command, and the ordering assertion holds. Same source as test.desc,
showing that only the memory type of the data register changes the outcome.
